<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolivian National Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1952</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bolivian Revolution of 1952</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bolivian National Revolution began in April 1952, when the Revolutionary Nationalist Movement (MNR) of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-paz-estenssoro">Víctor Paz Estenssoro</a>, backed by armed miners and workers, overthrew the military government. The new regime introduced universal suffrage, nationalised the large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> mines and carried out a sweeping land reform in 1953, transforming Bolivian society until the MNR was overthrown by a military coup in 1964.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolivian-national-revolution.jpg" alt="Bolivian National Revolution" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carwil Bjork-James · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Museum_of_National_Revolution_Bas_Relief.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
